        <div id="post-787" class="post-787 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-net category-testing category-visual-studio">

          <div class="post-header">
           <h3 class="post-title"><a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/2010/07/resharper-test-runner-and-mstest-projects/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: ReSharper Test Runner and MSTest Projects">ReSharper Test Runner and MSTest Projects</a></h3>
           <p class="post-date">
            <span class="month">Jul</span>
            <span class="day">21</span>
           </p>
           <p class="post-author">
            <span class="info">Posted by <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/author/cromwellryan/" title="Posts by cromwellryan ">cromwellryan</a> in <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/net/" title="View all posts in .Net" rel="category tag">.Net</a>, <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/testing/" title="View all posts in Testing" rel="category tag">Testing</a>, <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/visual-studio/" title="View all posts in Visual Studio" rel="category tag">Visual Studio</a> | <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/2010/07/resharper-test-runner-and-mstest-projects/#respond" class="comments"  title="Comment on ReSharper Test Runner and MSTest Projects"><span class="dsq-postid" rel="787 http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/index.php/2010/07/resharper-test-runner-and-mstest-projects/">View Comments</span></a>              </span>
           </p>
          </div>

          <div class="post-content clearfix">
          <p>One of my biggest irritants with the Unit Testing ecosystem is that each runner does things a little different. Gallio has helped solve this to some extent, but even that hasn’t solved all the problems that come with content or resource file deployments, coverage settings, etc.&#160; Gallio’s goal is noble if not arrogant, become the [...]</p>

